---
title: Sphenisciformes
---
# Sphenisciformes

Sphenisciformes is the order of penguins, flightless seabirds of the southern
hemisphere placed in the single family [[spheniscidae]]. The wing has been
reworked into a stiff, flattened flipper that beats against water rather than
air, and the bones are solid rather than pneumatic. Feathers are short, stiff
and densely overlapping, trapping a layer of air that insulates against water
near freezing. The group is old, with fossils from the late Cretaceous, and has
never occurred naturally north of the equator except in the Galapagos.
